          "body": "Bordeaux-Begles have been identified as a superior 'whole package' outfit compared to their southern hemisphere counterparts in a new ranking compiled by former England internationals Dan Cole and Ben Youngs. The double-winning Investec Champions Cup champions featured prominently in the analysis, which critically evaluated the current standard of Super Rugby Pacific. While the New Zealand-based Hurricanes were debated, the panel ultimately excluded them from the top 10, favouring the consistency and quality of the Top 14 teams."
