          "heading": "Owen Doyle condemns Michael Hooper and Sir Steve Hansen regarding Piardi",
          "body": "Former IRFU director of referees Owen Doyle has publicly criticised remarks made by Michael Hooper and Sir Steve Hansen concerning Italian official Andrea Piardi. The former Test referee dismissed the duo's recent suggestions that Piardi should no longer officiate matches involving Australia, labelling the commentary as \"totally out of order.\" Doyle defended the official's performance during the recent Wallabies-Springboks fixture, arguing that the officiating controversy stemmed from external communication failures rather than the referee’s decision-making on the pitch."
