          "heading": "Kieran Read urges Dave Rennie to build loose trio around Lakai",
          "body": "Former captain Kieran Read has identified Peter Lakai as the player the All Blacks must centre their back-row around for the upcoming Bledisloe Cup Tests. With Ardie Savea and Luke Jacobson sidelined due to injury, Read suggested that the team's loose forward combinations have lacked the time to solidify, noting that the pack is not yet settled on its best starting configuration. Read argued that Lakai offers the potential to provide the necessary stability to the All Blacks' loose forward unit."
